From be642a471b7674edd981b4843b11c18a4e4f1665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:01:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gallium/pvr: blit renders skip the full-target background
 load

A blit (used for mip generation, texture uploads of twiddled targets and get_handle copies) renders a
fullscreen quad that covers the whole target, but the flush still built the load background program
that samples the target's previous content - a full-target texture read and PDS load program per
blit, for pixels that are all overwritten. Use the clear background for blit renders instead, like
the depth-only path already does.

Measured on the X11/EGL glmark2 harness (same binary for all stacks, perf governor, cores 6-7, two
runs each): refract 36/36 -> 44/45 FPS (+23%; now level with zink's 47), terrain 20/20 -> 20/21,
shadow unchanged, full suite 729 -> 745 (+2.2%). Full gltri gate passes 49/49, 0 MMU faults.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c
index 0f6c974b..25c5debd 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_draw.c
@@ -1816,8 +1816,9 @@ pvr_draw_flush(struct pvr_context *ctx)
       goto done;
    uint64_t bgnd[3], pr_bgnd[3];
    /* Without a clear, the background reloads what the target held. A depth-only render drops the
-    * colour writes anyway, so it uses the (cheap) clear background instead of a full-target load. */
-   if (d->clear_valid || zonly || !draw_load_program(ctx, d, bgnd))
+    * colour writes anyway, and a blit's fullscreen quad covers the whole target, so both use the
+    * (cheap) clear background instead of a full-target load. */
+   if (d->clear_valid || zonly || d->load_src != NULL || !draw_load_program(ctx, d, bgnd))
       pvr_csb_pds_bgnd_words((uint32_t)bg, (uint32_t)bg, (uint32_t)bg, 0, 0, 0, bgnd);
    memcpy(pr_bgnd, bgnd, sizeof(bgnd));
    pvr_frag_static_stream_fill_bgnd(fstream, sizeof(fstream), d->bct_addr, bgnd, pr_bgnd);
-- 
